      "id": "CVE-2026-105806",
      "summary": "### Impact\nUnder certain conditions, an authenticated user could manage MCP API keys outside their intended account allowing an attacker to escalate privileges through account takeover.\n\nApplications that do not use `@payloadcms/plugin-mcp` are not affected.\n\n### Patches\nUsers should upgrade to `@payloadcms/plugin-mcp` version `3.88.0` or later.\n\n### Workarounds\nUpgrading is recommended. Until then, disable the MCP plugin or restrict MCP API-key management to trusted users.",
