    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-105845",
      "summary": "### Impact\nA user can submit a request that exploits a SQL Injection vulnerability in Payload.\n\nYou are affected if:\n- You use an affected Payload version.\n- Untrusted users can query readable collections using dynamic filters or joins.\n\nYou are not affected if you use MongoDB (`@payloadcms/mongodb`).\n\n### Patches\nUsers should upgrade Payload packages to `>= 3.88.0` or `>= 4.0.0-canary.27`.\n\n### Workarounds\nUpgrading to a patched version is recommended. Until you can upgrade, restrict untrusted users from supplying dynamic query filters or join parameters and limit read access to affected collections.",
